cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Public element sets against reconstructed orbits:
  a record-controlled reference benchmark
message: >-
  Cite this frozen paper and supporting-code release when using its measurements.
  The paper states the measured population, independent checks and limitations.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhana
    given-names: Nikhil
    email: "nikhilb9244@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2220-627X"
    city: "Cape Town"
    country: "ZA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikhilb9244-cloud/driftwatch"
url: "https://github.com/nikhilb9244-cloud/driftwatch/releases/tag/paper-2026-09-v2"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22661809"
abstract: >-
  Public SGP4 element sets are compared with reconstructed orbits for fifteen
  spacecraft at 460 to 1,338 km, with 1,193 usable sets and laser ranging as a
  further reference. The April 2024 control, May 2024, August 2024 held out and
  October 2024 held out windows have all been inspected. The paper reports
  record-controlled residual horizons, component coverage after covariance-basis
  transport, the completed September retrospective physical diagnostic,
  constructed topocentric crossing comparisons and two rejected learned
  propagators. It supersedes v1 at doi:10.5281/zenodo.22656992. These are
  measurements on the stated population, not operational guarantees.
keywords:
  - conjunction assessment
  - space situational awareness
  - SGP4
  - geomagnetic storm
  - thermospheric drag
  - orbit uncertainty
license: MIT
